  "hook": "80 million chips a day. India is entering the fab game.",
  "headline": "India Targets 80M Chips Per Day by Late 2026",
  "body": [
    "India is set to reach 80 million semiconductor chips per day in production capacity by late 2026, marking a historic entry into global chip manufacturing.",
    "Four facilities are driving this transformation: Tata Electronics in Assam for assembly and testing, Micron in Gujarat for memory packaging, CG Power for outsourced assembly and test (OSAT), and RRP Electronics for compound semiconductors.",
    "The combined investment across these four plants totals $15.2 billion, with 28,000 direct jobs expected once all facilities reach commercial scale.",
    "India Semiconductor Mission coordinates the national strategy, leveraging PLI incentives and state partnerships to accelerate timelines across all four projects."
  ],
  "insight": "India moves from zero domestic chip production to 80 million units per day in under three years, backed by $15.2B in committed capital across four facilities.",
